  "query_preview": "..\n\nUpper ridging on Sunday will begin to flatten into a zonal flow\nregime across eastern Montana and the Northern High Plains Sunday\nnight into Monday. This will guide west surface winds Sunday\nafternoon across the area which may be gusty at times, but may\nstay shy of Lake Wind Criteria for Fort Peck Lake.\n\nA fast moving shortwave will eject out of the Pacific Northwest\nand over the Northern Rockies and into eastern Montana and Wyoming\nMonday night and Tuesday. This will likely result in increased\ncloud cover and perhaps a stray shower, though most ensembles keep\nsteadiest QPF to the southwest of the CWA.\n\nEnsembles show a large high amplitude upper ridge becoming\nestablished over the western CONUS for the second half of the week\nwhich will result in prominent dry weather conditions and warmer\ntemperatures as highs return to the 50s and 60s for much of NE\nMontana.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM held the line this forecast cycle with above average\nconfidence for mostly dry weather this week. The exception is\nMonday night into Tuesday with some uncertainty in precip chances\nas that shortwave approaches. For now expect most places will see\nlittle if any measurable rainfall. Despite longer time ranges,\nensembles are in full support of rebounding ridging late in the\nweek, helping to guide dry and milder weather for the region.",
